; Saved copy of Willy's state: the position he returns to after a death
;
; 7 bytes, a copy of $85CF-$85D5 made at every room entry (#R$8912, at $894A), before the room is built:
; +0 Y index #R$85CF
; .
; +1 move state #R$85D0
; .
; +2 air state #R$85D1
; .
; +3 walk frame #R$85D2
; .
; +4 attribute address #R$85D3 (word, low byte first)
; .
; +6 jump step #R$85D5
; .
; When Willy is killed and a life is left, #R$8B07 (at $8C3C) copies the 7 bytes back and enters the room
; again, so he restarts from the state in which he entered it (a room entered by falling in restarts
; the fall). The rope variable #R$85D6 is not part of the copy.
; .
; Observed (finding F117): after entering a room with Willy in the middle of a walk (state 3, frame 2, jump step 5)
; and a fatal fall, all seven variables came back with the saved values.
@label=WillySavedState
g$85D7 DEFB $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00
